{"path":"experimental/fs/canonical","title":"std::experimental::filesystem::canonical","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::filesystem::</span>canonical","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/fs/canonical","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"Converts path p to a canonical absolute path, i.e. an absolute path that has no dot, dot-dot elements or symbolic links.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/experimental/filesystem\">&lt;experimental/filesystem&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-fs_ts\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">path canonical<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> base <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> current_path<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-fs-ts t-mark-ts\">(filesystem TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-fs_ts\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">path canonical<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p, error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> ec <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-fs-ts t-mark-ts\">(filesystem TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-fs_ts\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">path canonical<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> base, error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> ec <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-fs-ts t-mark-ts\">(filesystem TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Converts path <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> to a canonical absolute path, i.e. an absolute path that has no dot, dot-dot elements or symbolic links.\n</p><p>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> is not an absolute path, the function behaves as if it is first made absolute by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">absolute<span class=\"br0\">(</span>p, base<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">absolute<span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> for <span class=\"t-v\">(2)</span>.\n</p><p>The path <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> must exist.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> p\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> a path which may be absolute or relative to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">base</span></code>, and which must be an existing path\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> base\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> base path to be used in case <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> is relative\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> ec\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> error code to store error status to\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>An absolute path that resolves to the same file as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">absolute<span class=\"br0\">(</span>p, base<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> (or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">absolute<span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> for <span class=\"t-v\">(2)</span>).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\nThe overload that does not take an <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span></code> parameter throws <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/fs/filesystem_error\">filesystem_error</a> on underlying OS API errors, constructed with <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> as the first argument, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">base</span></code> as the second argument, and the OS error code as the error code argument. <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\"><span class=\"kw698\">std::<span class=\"me2\">bad_alloc</span></span></a></span></code> may be thrown if memory allocation fails. The overload taking an <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span></code> parameter sets it to the OS API error code if an OS API call fails, and executes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ec.<span class=\"me1\">clear</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> if no errors occur. This overload has <div class=\"t-noexcept-inline\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/language/noexcept_spec\"><code>noexcept</code></a> specification:&nbsp;&nbsp;<div class=\"t-noexcept-box\"><span class=\"t-cc\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span></span></span></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</div>\n<p>This function is modeled after the POSIX <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/functions/realpath.html\" data-external=\"1\">realpath</a>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;experimental/filesystem&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> fs <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">filesystem</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span> p <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"..\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"..\"</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"AppData\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Current path is \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">current_path</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Canonical path for \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> p <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" is \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">canonical</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Current path is \"C:\\Users\\abcdef\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\"\nCanonical path for \"..\\..\\AppData\" is \"C:\\Users\\abcdef\\AppData\"</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/fs/path\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>path</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  represents a path <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/fs/absolute\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>absolute</span><span>system_complete</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  composes an absolute path<br>converts a path to an absolute path replicating OS-specific behavior <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/fs","title":"Filesystem library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::filesystem::canonical","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"3 declarations. Converts path p to a canonical absolute path, i.e. an absolute path that has no dot, dot-dot elements or symbolic links."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"p, base, ec"},{"label":"Return value","note":"An absolute path that resolves to the same file as absolute(p, base) (or absolute(p) for (2))."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"The overload that does not take an"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"path","note":"represents a path"},{"label":"absolute, system_complete","note":"composes an absolute pathconverts a path to an absolute path replicating OS-specific behavior"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":320,"codeBlockCount":2}
